+  Rule: DOM node identity is preserved across state changes
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a single todo keeps its DOM node alive
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user notes the DOM node for todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the tracked DOM node is still the same element
+      And the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" does not have the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Toggling all keeps every DOM node alive
+      Given the following todos exist:
